        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "My son's Minecraft server has been running in our data center for 18 months.\n\nI built it for his birthday because my home internet was too slow.\n\nThe company had an unused server with 256GB of RAM.\n\nHe had six friends.\n\nThis seemed efficient.\n\nLast month our infrastructure team noticed one machine generating constant outbound traffic to residential IPs after 4 PM.\n\nSecurity asked what application lived on it.\n\nI said it was a Java-based distributed collaboration environment.\n\nThey asked who owned it.\n\nI said a small external user group.\n\nNobody asked the next question.\n\nInstead, engineering requested access because they thought I had built an internal sandbox platform.\n\nI gave them a separate instance.\n\nNow 32 developers use it for testing.\n\nThe CTO approved two new servers for “non-production experimentation.”\n\nMy son just got upgraded to 512GB of RAM.\n\nHappy early birthday."
        },
